Z||000000||AutoXdbdragSE||11-06-2001||12:14 AM||||Ok, i was just messing with my comp, and all of a sudden IE displayed everything with big fonts.. how do i change it.. i've tried windows settings.. that didn't work,  IE settings.. no help there, how can i go back to normal sized fonts.. <BR>example.. on this page..everything is freaking huge... how can i get rid of this problem<BR>thanks in advance||||reg||1
Z||000001||frontal lobe||11-06-2001||01:24 AM||||Try holding the control (Ctrl) button on your keyboard down while scrolling your mouse.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||11-06-2001||07:47 AM||||frontal lobe gave you the short cut. Use View on the menu, then Text Size.<P>Unfortunatly not all forums support this feature but Pennock's does.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||11-06-2001||09:27 AM||||It isn't a forum feature. It is an IE net feature.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||11-06-2001||09:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>It isn't a forum feature. It is an IE net feature.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not entirely true, sites can override the IE default font size if they use <B>absolute</B> font sizes.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SteveJ||11-06-2001||11:02 AM||||Those of us whose eyesight is not all it could be appreciate the larger font sizes. I don't have to put on my glasses and sit 12 inches from the screen.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Return of Fiero||11-06-2001||08:08 PM||||i have th oposite problem, my fonts ar small on some pages, and i cant figure it out. wife was playing with aol, and now i cant get the lettering back to normal. the letters are so small i cant read them half the time. any takers?<BR>Myke||||reg||1
Z||000007||BC-GT||11-06-2001||09:06 PM||||Well, if you go to tools, Internet options, accessibility, you can override the absolute font size that web site creators can use(or so it says) "Specifies whether you want Internet Explorer to always use the default font size you choose. You can set the default font size on the General tab by clicking the Fonts button. If the author of a Web page chooses a different default font size, the settings you choose here will override it. You cannot change the size or color of graphics."<P><P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||AutoXdbdragSE||11-07-2001||12:42 AM||||thanks guys the CTRL scroll thing worked||||reg||1
